---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";

---

<Layout title="resources">
    <section class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-muted">
        <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
            <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.3em] text-slate-500 dark:text-muted-foreground">Resources</p>
            <h1>References I keep coming back to</h1>
            <p>
                This is a secondary page on purpose: a small collection of learning resources that have been useful for
                sharpening specific skills and technical judgment.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="rounded border-8 border-double border-black bg-background dark:border-border dark:bg-card dark:text-card-foreground">
        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold">Great Frontend</h3>
                <p class="mt-2">A strong resource for refreshing front-end fundamentals, practicing interviews, and seeing React and browser concepts explained clearly.</p>
                <p class="mt-3">Link: <a class="underline" href="https://www.greatfrontend.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">greatfrontend.com</a></p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold">Java</h3>
                <p class="mt-2">The University of Helsinki's <a class="underline" href="https://java-programming.mooc.fi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Java Programming</a> course is the main structured resource I use when I want rigor and repetition.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold">C++</h3>
                <p class="mt-2">The <a class="underline" href="https://www.learncpp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Learn C++</a> site is especially useful because it meets beginners where they are while still explaining how lower-level language mechanics actually work.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <h3 class="font-semibold">PlatformIO</h3>
                <p class="mt-2"><a class="underline" href="https://platformio.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PlatformIO</a> has been my preferred entry point for embedded experimentation because it feels much closer to the tooling expectations I already have from web development.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>
